\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10 -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/des.md\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/ids.txt\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/prompt.md\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:19:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/prompt.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:20:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/prompt.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n\\\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n\\\\n参考题目如下：\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"88e364bc\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"102-115\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\\\\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\\\\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\\\\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"6cbe9eb8\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"79-94\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\\\\n- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\\\\n- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\\\\n- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\\\\n- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"230f2e48\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"19-38\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nFold each straight red rod at its black marker, leaving the gray-anchored side fixed.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- Each foreground object is a straight horizontal or vertical 4-connected rod.\\\\n- Each rod contains many pixels of one line color, one endpoint marker, and one\\\\n  interior control marker.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- For every rod, keep the segment from the endpoint marker through the control\\\\n  marker unchanged.\\\\n- Move the line-color tail on the far side of the control marker to a\\\\n  perpendicular ray starting next to that marker.\\\\n- Choose the perpendicular direction with more space to the grid edge.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The endpoint marker identifies the fixed side of the rod, while the control\\\\n  marker is the hinge; the tail folds into the larger open half-plane.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"b7256dcd\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"18-32\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nTransfer each colored marker to its adjacent neutral mask component, then erase the markers.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the most common color.\\\\n- The neutral mask color is the unique most frequent foreground color.\\\\n- Other foreground colors are marker pixels that may touch neutral 4-connected mask components.\\\\nRule\\\\n- Remove every marker pixel by recoloring it to the background.\\\\n- For each 4-connected neutral mask component, find marker colors touching it by edge adjacency.\\\\n- If a component touches one marker color, recolor the whole neutral component to that marker color.\\\\n- If a component touches no marker color, leave it neutral.\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- Marker pixels label neighboring neutral regions but are not part of the final colored objects.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"458e3a53\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"19-32\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExtract the compact table of solid cells hidden inside a separator lattice.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The grid has full-width and full-height bars of one separator color, dividing it into rectangular cells.\\\\n- Most cells contain a repeating multicolor pattern, while a contiguous rectangle of cells is solid monochrome.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Split the input into lattice cells using the full separator rows and columns.\\\\n- Keep the cells whose full interior is one color, crop to their occupied rectangle, and output those colors.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The periodic pattern is noise; only completely solid lattice cells encode the reduced output grid.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"db695cfb\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"8-19\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nConnect same-color diagonal pixel pairs, then emit perpendicular rays from differently-colored pixels on those diagonals.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color. Line color (e.g. blue) has pixel pairs aligned on shared diagonals. Trigger color (e.g. magenta) pixels sit along those diagonals.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Draw diagonal lines connecting each pair of same-color aligned pixels.\\\\n- Where the diagonal crosses a trigger pixel, emit perpendicular diagonal rays (in the trigger's color) extending to the grid boundary.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Trigger pixels act as beam-splitters — the perpendicular rays rotate 90° from the connecting diagonal's orientation.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"25c199f5\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"30-44\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPack the non-background rows from three separated panels into one panel, scanning panels right-to-left.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- A rectangular grid contains three equal-size panels separated by two full-height divider columns.\\\\n- The background is the dominant color; divider pixels use a color that appears only in the divider columns.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Read panels from right to left, and within each panel read rows from top to bottom.\\\\n- Keep each row that contains any non-background pixel, discarding all-background rows.\\\\n- Place the kept rows at the bottom of a single panel-shaped output, padding above with background rows.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The task is row packing: the divider columns mark independent panels, and only the occupied rows are moved.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"99caaf76\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"56-75\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMove each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color\\\\n  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.\\\\n- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly\\\\n  one side of the cross.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object\\\\n  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.\\\\n- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.\\\\n- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\nThe marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,\\\\nand only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"db0c5428\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"32-51\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExpand a 3x3 block motif into a 5x5 block motif around its missing center.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Teal background surrounds one 9x9 foreground motif.\\\\n- The motif is a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks; the middle block is empty teal.\\\\n- Colored pixels immediately around the empty middle block encode the border\\\\n  of the missing center block.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Keep the original 9x9 motif in place.\\\\n- Copy each of the eight surrounding 3x3 blocks to the opposite outer slot\\\\n  of the implied 5x5 block grid, without rotating it.\\\\n- Fill the center block from the eight pixels around the hole; its center is\\\\n  the motif's majority foreground color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The visible 9x9 motif is the middle of a larger periodic\\\\nblock-level pattern, and the empty center is reconstructed from its immediate\\\\ninner boundary.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"e3721c99\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"69-83\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRecolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.\\\\n- Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,\\\\n  each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.\\\\n- For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).\\\\n- Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"11\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"8698868d\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"9-23\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMatch sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.\\\\n- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Frames form a regular grid; some may be bg-colored (invisible).\\\\n- Count connected hole regions inside each frame's interior and each sprite.\\\\n- Pair each frame with the sprite sharing the same hole count.\\\\n- Place the matched sprite inside the frame border; recolor sprite holes to the frame's color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The matching key is the number of connected hole components, not hole area or color.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"12\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"0934a4d8\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"75-90\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:21:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"if [ -f /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/10/1.py ]; then sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/10/1.py; else echo MISSING; fi\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:22:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"if [ -f /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2627817